{#-
  The two printed pages, as markup. Rendered by BOTH templates
  (templates/brief.html.j2 = print-first A4, templates/mobile.html.j2 = responsive).

  Keeping the page markup in one partial is deliberate: the printed newspaper must be
  the same document whichever source produced it, so only the CSS differs between the
  two artefacts.

  Three structural rules, each learned from a defect this page actually had:

  1. NO CSS multi-column (`columns:`) inside a fixed-height page box. A multicol
     container that cannot fit fragments into new columns — in paged media that means
     additional pages — so content is either dropped silently (the page box has
     `overflow: hidden`) or painted over itself. Neither shows up in `scrollHeight`,
     so neither is caught by a layout measurement.
  2. Columns on page two are explicit stack elements whose contents are assigned by
     code (pipeline.content.plan_inside_columns), because the natural section order
     does not pack into two fixed-height columns: it wastes a fifth of the page and
     ends up 1017px into a 1018px column.
  3. Only section-lead stories print a deck and a dateline, and citations are inline
     attributions rather than their own lines. Thirteen of either does not fit two A4
     columns; config.budgets is calibrated against the worst case that does.

  Context required: e (edition content), meta (code-generated metadata),
  assets (inlined, trusted SVG), titles (section display names), inside_plan
  (code-computed section-to-column assignment).
-#}
{% import "_macros.j2" as macros %}
{% set lead_paras = e.lead.paras | length %}
{% set lead_split = ((lead_paras + 1) // 2) if lead_paras > 2 else lead_paras %}
{% set plan = inside_plan if (inside_plan is defined and inside_plan) else {'left': ['technology', 'sport'], 'right': ['finance', 'culture']} %}
<main>
<section class="page page--front" id="page-1" aria-label="Front page">
<header class="masthead">
<div class="masthead-ornament" aria-hidden="true">{{ assets['masthead-ornament'] }}</div>
<h1 class="masthead-title">The Global Brief</h1>
<p class="masthead-meta">
<span class="masthead-date">{{ meta.date_long }}</span><span class="masthead-sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span><span class="masthead-edition">{{ meta.edition_label }}</span><span class="masthead-sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span><span class="masthead-issue">No. {{ meta.edition_number }}</span>
</p>
<p class="masthead-window">{{ meta.window_line }} · {{ meta.sources_cited }} sources cited</p>
</header>

<div class="page-body page-body--front">
<div class="front-band front-band--top">
<article class="story story--lead" id="lead">
{{ macros.headline_block(e.lead, 'lead-headline', titles['geopolitics']) }}
<div class="lead-body">
<div class="lead-col">{{ macros.para_block(e.lead, 'story-paras', 0, lead_split) }}</div>
<div class="lead-col">{{ macros.para_block(e.lead, 'story-paras', lead_split) }}</div>
</div>
{{ macros.source_line(e.lead) }}
</article>
<aside class="front-rail">
{{ macros.visual_block(assets['wire-globe'], meta.visual_caption) }}
{{ macros.briefs_panel(e.briefs, 'Briefs') }}
</aside>
</div>

<div class="front-band front-band--bottom" id="markets">
{% for item in e.secondary %}
{{ macros.story_block(item, titles['geopolitics'], 'secondary-headline', 'story-paras', true, 'story story--secondary') }}
{% endfor %}
{{ macros.markets_panel(e.markets, 'Markets') }}
</div>
</div>

{{ macros.page_footer(meta.footer_text, 'Page 1 of 2') }}
</section>

<section class="page page--inside" id="page-2" aria-label="Page 2">
<div class="inside-head">
<span class="inside-head-title">{{ meta.inside_title }}</span>
<span class="inside-head-note">{{ meta.inside_note }}</span>
</div>

<div class="page-body page-body--inside">
<div class="inside-column inside-column--left">
{% for section_id in plan['left'] %}
{{ macros.inside_section(section_id, e, titles) }}
{% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="inside-column inside-column--right">
{% for section_id in plan['right'] %}
{{ macros.inside_section(section_id, e, titles) }}
{% endfor %}
</div>
</div>

{{ macros.page_footer(meta.footer_text, 'Page 2 of 2') }}
</section>
</main>
